            $TRANS$If a consumer applies to examine his case before the Exceptions Committee under clause (b3), during the period specified in subparagraph (f), and before the committee's decision has been made in his case, an essential service provider will be entitled to operate a collection tool at least 12 days from the date of the committee's decision, and he may do so even if the period stated in subparagraph (f) has not yet passed." (4) In addition to the provisions of paragraph (3), with respect to a consumer debt at a household rate, the following provisions shall apply: Throughout the collection process under paragraph (3), if the date for the issuance of a new consumer account has arrived at the place of consumption, the account will be generated in the regular procedure as specified in Principle 21 and in this Standard;$TRANS$
