            $TRANS$A default provider will send a notice to a consumer who has received accounts by mail about the transition to sending bills by email; The notice will be sent by means listed in the True Measure 5, at least two months before the transfer is made. A default provider will allow consumers whose email address is not registered with the supplier's office to provide it in a circular. The account will be deemed to have been delivered to a registered consumer by any digital means according to the details provided by the registered consumer to the default provider for this purpose. An account sent to a registered consumer, via e-mail, will be credited with the cost set out in line 26 of the tariff schedule 2-5.4.$TRANS$
