            '2026-01-12T21:12:01.566000+00:00',
            $TRANS$Handling a complaint for a real read invoice when the corresponding period is not in a real read In the case of a complaint about a specific invoice based on a real read, when the invoice from the corresponding period is based on a non-real read, the following checks must be performed: i.e. – a complaint about a specific invoice whose read type is a real read and the type of read in the invoice in the corresponding period is not genuine. Therefore, we will perform the following tests: Checking the type of reading in the corresponding period If the previous corresponding period is based on an untrue reading, we will not make a comparison due to the concern of distorting the daily average between the periods. If there is an additional invoice after the invoice that the customer pays for, it will be possible to compare it to the repair period in the previous year (i.e., the calculation must be for the same periods in the case of a repair invoice) – in other words, I have a period of four months that I can compare to four months in the previous year because the additional invoice in the previous year is a repair invoice. We will be happy for confirmation - the customer complained about a real invoice - check whether the invoice from last year after it is real or not. If it's real, is there another invoice after the invoice he complained about?$TRANS$
        );
    END IF;
END $chunk_fn$;


