            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "אפיון עסקי - בדיקות מוצר.docx", "file_type": "docx", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "59c9109b-48af-4854-9747-4d34e36c8935", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "c54aad3b1a0cba4027f315540112f7fd", "create_date": "2026-01-12T21:12:01.570Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/c54aad3b1a0cba4027f315540112f7fd/data/1768252310218-אפיון עסקי - בדיקות מוצר.docx", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: חשבון תיקון, קריאה אמיתית, תקופת חיוב, דילוגים, חשבונית חשמל"}}'::jsonb,
            '2026-01-12T21:12:01.570000+00:00',
            $TRANS$* When a "Repair" account appears, it is usually a real call made after an assessment period, or in a situation that is explicitly stated in the "Account Correction" invoice.* A Repair Account usually includes a wider billing period (sometimes several months), which includes dates that have already appeared on previous invoices. In the event that there are several consecutive skips, the number of skips and the amount of the credit must be indicated, if there are several skips but not consecutive, the agent must present a note to the handler that includes the number of skips in the last 6 invoices in a bi-monthly account or 12 invoices in a one-month account, and in any case provide a response to send to the customer.* The number of skips should not be specified, but only the period in which the skip was made.  It should be clarified that the correction invoice reflects the actual consumption in accordance with the reading made after the skip period. It should be noted for every notice that relates to a high electricity bill in the amendment, it should be noted that, in the electricity bills generated based on an estimate reading, it is clearly recorded, in red font, that: "The bill is submitted according to the estimate. The meter status can be provided in the 103 service or on the website.$TRANS$
        );
    END IF;
END $chunk_fn$;


