            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "אפיון עסקי - בדיקות מוצר.docx", "file_type": "docx", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "73b48e8c-75c6-47d5-8fce-d95726c8a1d9", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "c54aad3b1a0cba4027f315540112f7fd", "create_date": "2026-01-12T21:12:01.563Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/c54aad3b1a0cba4027f315540112f7fd/data/1768252310218-אפיון עסקי - בדיקות מוצר.docx", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: מונה חכם, מונה בסיסי, חברת חשמל, זיהוי מונה, קריאת מונה"}}'::jsonb,
            '2026-01-12T21:12:01.563000+00:00',
            $TRANS$In order to implement the test, the customer will be able to contact the IEC's 103 hotline, via the website, chat or digital form at the following link: https://www.iec.co.il/pages/reqnoident.aspx C. Meter Type TestThe system will perform a test to identify the customer's meter type: Smart Meter / Basic Meter. The data is taken from the "Historical Meter Reading Data" screen, from the Smart Counter1 field. Basic Counter Identification (Non-Smart) If the Smart Counter field is empty (no value appears), it is a non-smart meter (basic counter) There may be an exceptional situation in which the customer has an actual smart meter installed, but the call is carried out by an external supplier, due to a malfunction in the meter and its transfer to a manual reading track. In such a situation, the system will treat it as a basic meter for the process. 2. Smart Counter Identification If the Smart Count field contains the value "Smart Meter exists": This is a smart meter in this case, if an invoice is in the estimation/skip status: the agent will present a message to the handling representative, clarifying that the customer has a smart meter.$TRANS$
        );
    END IF;
END $chunk_fn$;


