            '2026-01-12T21:12:01.565000+00:00',
            $TRANS$Verify the reading type on the "Invoices" screen that the reading type is a real reading (detailed reading table) B. Locate an invoice from a parallel period in the previous year for comparison C. Calculate and compare consumption If the invoice from the corresponding period is based on a real reading, a calculation must be performed in order to check the consumption deviation, according to the following formula: (If the reading is not real, we will move to section D)Total consumption of the invoice from the corresponding period / billing days in the corresponding period = the average daily consumption in the corresponding period ( A new figure that you get in the calculation of the corresponding period)*The same calculation is also performed for the specific invoice for the current period. If a change of more than 20% in consumption compared to the corresponding period is detected, the system will automatically notify the Ombudsman for examination and confirmation that there has indeed been a drastic change in the customer's consumption compared to the previous year. In this type of case, the agent will provide a response without reference to the amount of the deviation and will send a notice to the handling party in the form of a letter to the employee: Please note that if a consumption deviation exceeding 20% has been identified between two periods, the source of the deviation must be investigated.$TRANS$
        );
    END IF;
END $chunk_fn$;


