            '2026-01-12T21:12:01.571000+00:00',
            $TRANS$You can report an updated meter reading through the 103 chat call center, on the IEC's website or on WhatsApp at 055-7000103, after which a correction invoice will be issued reflecting the actual consumption.  and the information is provided to the customer as part of the aforementioned response in cases where there is a sequence of skips. The invoices contain two possible types of compensation: "Periodic non-reading credit of the meter in a row / 3 times a year" "Credit for periodic non-reading of the meter" The total number of credits appearing in the invoices in which skips were made must be calculated, and the total amount must be presented to the customer as part of the response related to the correction period as aforesaid in cases where there is a sequence of skips, in case there is no sequence, a message will be presented to the representative that includes the number of skips that includes the number of skips in the last 6 invoices in a bi-monthly account or 12 invoices in the account Monthly and the amount the customer received. We would be happy to refine the formulation 2.0 High Electricity Bill – without a specific invoice.$TRANS$
        );
