            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "אפיון עסקי - בדיקות מוצר.docx", "file_type": "docx", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "d9b6d7e1-f725-40b7-916b-f6f2601dbf52", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "c54aad3b1a0cba4027f315540112f7fd", "create_date": "2026-01-12T21:12:01.570Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/c54aad3b1a0cba4027f315540112f7fd/data/1768252310218-אפיון עסקי - בדיקות מוצר.docx", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: חשבונית, קריאה אמיתית, חישוב, ממוצע יומי, חשבון חשמל"}}'::jsonb,
            '2026-01-12T21:12:01.570000+00:00',
            $TRANS$As soon as there is no subsequent invoice for the invoice he complained about, then the second option – another option is to check 3 invoices (the same period, a previous invoice and an invoice after that), provided that at least two of the invoices are according to regular reading. If there are no two invoices in the real reading, a message will be presented to the employee, we will be happy to refine the wording – there is no wording yet, the subject is new and has not yet been used, if it is real – we will proceed to the next calculation – performing the calculation if there is a real reading. We will calculate the daily average meter reading from the same period last year (estimated) + a real sequential invoice between the meter reading of the correction invoice and the meter reading of the real invoice for the same period (year back) b. Multiply the value of the daily average by the number of days of the evaluation invoice. We can then make the required comparison according to the calculation described in section 1.1c, against the average daily consumption on the invoice for which the customer complained. We would be happy to refine the wording 1.3 High Electricity Bill - Repair Invoice* IEC is allowed to perform a "skip" twice a year.$TRANS$
        );
    END IF;
