            $TRANS$Rejection Repair: Making adjustments and improvements to the system in accordance with the feedback collected during the pilot, while correcting malfunctions, improving the user experience, and ensuring optimal system functioning. C. Establishment and management of two work environments (test and production: subject to IEC infrastructures) For the purpose of controlled implementation and ongoing and safe management of the system, two separate work environments will be established: a test/pilot environment (Test/UAT) and a production environment. D. Upgrade to a production environment: After completing the necessary repairs and approvals, a gradual increase will be carried out to the production environment and the expansion of use to all employees of the department, in accordance with the order of magnitude that will be defined in advance. Part 2 – Use Cases and Treatment MethodologyThis chapter will present practical examples from previous cases, in order to illustrate the desired way of operating the system. The purpose of this section is to learn from previous experience, identify possible failures in advance, and ensure that the planned solution provides the best response to the needs identified in the project. Types of inquiries: A tree that presents the scope of the project (the initial one – will be expanded later) within the content world of "high electricity bill" inquiries.$TRANS$
