            $TRANS$Content Part 1 – Background and Objectives of the Project 2 Goals and Objectives 2 Target Audience 3 The Implementation Process 3 Part 2 – Use Cases and Treatment Methodology 4 1.0 High Electricity Bill – Specific Invoice 6 1.2 Specific Invoice Untrue Reading 8 1.3 High Electricity Bill – Correction Invoice 9 2.0 High Electricity Bill – Without Specific Invoice 10 3.0 Inquiry Due to Fluctuations in the Electricity Bill 11 The Benchmark Table – To add to the extent and absence of relevant criteria for the scope of the project. 12 Part C - Visual documentation of the data 13 Part A - Background and objectives of the projectBackgroundThe Public Complaints Unit in the Service Division, a supply division at the IEC handles many inquiries relating to consumption bills, meter measurements, irregular charges, and various malfunctions. Today, the work process is carried out manually and requires employees to perform many data cross-references, calculations, and technical checks, relying on professional knowledge. In addition, the wording of the response varies among the representatives and is not uniform, which harms the consistency and uniformity of service to the public. This situation causes operational congestion, delays in handling inquiries, and a clear need to streamline processes, standardize the response, and improve the service experience for both employees and customers.$TRANS$
