            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.291000+00:00',
            $TRANS$We will find the following redirects: (should be done for the bigram $l d$) lo → alone → lore → sloth or → border → lore → morbid rd → ardent → border → card It is better to take the words that contain the maximum sequences, in our case: lore and border. We will try to calculate the degree of correspondence between the query word and these two words. For this purpose, we will use a coefficient called Jaccard Coefficient. The coefficient checks for an overlap between two groups A and B: 푗푎푐푐푎푟푑 푐표푒푓푓푖푐푖푒푛푡= |퐴∩퐵| |퐴푈퐵|   When the groups are sorted, the complexity depends on the size of the longest list.$TRANS$
