            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.379000+00:00',
            $TRANS$The writers of the pages are not trained writers. • The content of the pages can contain errors, lies, contradictions, duplicates. • There is no simple answer to the question "How big is the Internet"? In order to try to understand this, we will look at the pages and divide them into two parts: • Static pages – pages that do not change from one request to another (html pages) • Dynamic pages – pages that are created by a server in response to a query to the databases (PHP pages).  You can look at static pages together with the links within them as a directed graph, where each web page is a node and the link is an arc or a side.$TRANS$
