            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "סיכום למבחן אחזור מידע (1).pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "2fc2f204-002a-4903-aa2e-ddb115e93303", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808", "create_date": "2025-08-26T11:29:00.275Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808/data/1756207659351-0c8cd1917d00e951630029e4978e9147.pdf", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: חיתוך, מושגים, רשימות, תרגיל, שאילתה"}}'::jsonb,
            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.275000+00:00',
            $TRANS$Taking a step to find the cut between the two, we will save 1 in the product and compare it against the dog's list in order to find the cut between the three lists. Exercise number 2 What two concepts should you start with? The concepts in parentheses are considered as one concept, we will consider their size, for example tangerine or trees we will get 363,456. According to the calculation, we will upload the two shortest lists and make the cut between them: tangerine, trees, kaleidoscope, eyes. Exercise number 3 according to the query: Paris and not (France or Lear) so in the end we will be left with: 6, 10. How do you move from a collection of houses to signs?$TRANS$
