            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.341000+00:00',
            $TRANS$We will perform searches in an index that saves the position of the concept in the document, and thus we will be able to give more importance to documents in which the terms appear at a high level of proximity (we will give a low index). Query Parsers divides the query in a different way before sending it to the search engine and can connect all the results. Suppose we run the following query: Rising interest rates In the first step, we will search for all the concepts as a single unit in a position-saving index. If the number of documents is not sufficient, we will look for two combinations: rising interest and interest rates. If the number of documents is still insufficient, we will look for the three words separately.$TRANS$
