            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.381000+00:00',
            $TRANS$• It is estimated that 40% of the pages are copies of other pages, even in the world of articles we can see copies in one form or another. • Many of these copies are legal copies in order to maintain surplus and reliability. • Search engines try to avoid indexing copies of the same content. How do we identify duplicates? Let's say we want to identify a duplicate document, for each document we assign a signature based on a hash function that translates the content into some number, and compare signatures. If two documents are signed identically, we can declare them as copies. There is a problem that documents are almost copies. Why do replicas create a problem?$TRANS$
