            $TRANS$The question arises as to which of the two metrics is better, we can see that the Document Frequency index shows a difference between the two words that we understand that there needs to be a difference between these words (it is likely that try will be less rare than Insurance).   The prevalence of a collection of documents can be great as a result of the high prevalence of a relevant document and not as a result of the fact that the concept is common. Rare vs. Common Concepts A rare concept provides more information than a common concept. A rare concept, appears in fewer documents, i.e. t df will be low.$TRANS$
