            89,
            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "סיכום למבחן אחזור מידע (1).pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "b61873bc-2091-4e37-baeb-5199ff5ecb0a", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808", "create_date": "2025-08-26T11:29:00.332Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808/data/1756207659351-0c8cd1917d00e951630029e4978e9147.pdf", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: מושג, שאילתה, מסמכים, ציונים, יעילות"}}'::jsonb,
            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.332000+00:00',
            $TRANS$In the course, we will assume that each concept appears once in the query, and no other weight is given to a particular concept in the query (for example, for Hanukkah it is not said in advance that Hanukkah is more important than a holiday, only the weights will determine the weight of each word). • We will search for k best documents We have N documents, of which J documents appear in the posting list of concepts. We will look for the k documents with the best grades from J. We will need to specify the J scores, the sorting will be efficiently O(JlogJ). We can improve the efficiency of sorting to O(J) by using the data structure stack.$TRANS$
