            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "סיכום למבחן אחזור מידע (1).pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "c52d3f67-e22d-44a1-8c2e-6b1cdf9f5b2f", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808", "create_date": "2025-08-26T11:29:00.384Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808/data/1756207659351-0c8cd1917d00e951630029e4978e9147.pdf", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: חתימה, מידע, זיכרון, מסמך, מטריצה בוליאנית"}}'::jsonb,
            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.384000+00:00',
            $TRANS$The signature reduces the amount of information that needs to be stored in memory. In our example, we will create a signature for each sequence, so that we take a document and represent it as a set of signatures (instead of a set of letters or words). The basic model of a document is represented by a set of signatures of sequences. We will mark: the set of sequences of the document j d- (j S(d (the sequences of the words or letters themselves) The set of sequence signatures of the document j d- ) j H(d) We will enter the set of signatures of the sequences into a Boolean matrix. S stands for the screen (like d.)  The values in the table will be 1 or 0, 1 when the sequence appears and 0 when the sequence does not appear.$TRANS$
