            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.393000+00:00',
            $TRANS$If we take out a URL that sits on a Microsoft site and give it to its crawler that has the ability to work in parallel, and let it work on another URL from the same computer, that crawler will eventually be bombed. When the search engine goes to index a page of a certain server, it constantly turns to its server and interferes with it, so we want to avoid maximum disruption. We will be able to see the URLs that enter the queue, there is a front queue and a back queue, and at the end we will retrieve the URL for treatment not according to first in, first out, but according to a more sophisticated method. Only after going through both layers can we retrieve a suitable URL.$TRANS$
