            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "סיכום למבחן אחזור מידע (1).pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "cc356b80-38d4-4685-865a-4d0770ded220", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808", "create_date": "2025-08-26T11:29:00.388Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808/data/1756207659351-0c8cd1917d00e951630029e4978e9147.pdf", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: Hash, מסמכים, פרמוטציות, חתימות, זחלן אינטרנט"}}'::jsonb,
            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.388000+00:00',
            $TRANS$The hash represents that in the end documents that are similar will be similar in the different permutations. We can see that we originally did the index on all 7 comparisons between the words, the claim is that this is equivalent to calculating the index for the permutations we received on the signatures (with a slight incitement in the results) we will compare the two methods of the hash and the jaccard, we can see that the hash is less accurate than the jaccard index, but if we do this enough times we will get a similar sample. Web crawler in this lesson will see what architecture the search engine uses to reach a large number of pages.$TRANS$
