            $TRANS$• There is an assumption that the dictionary of term-termID can be held in the main memory. • If the number of concepts is very large so that this assumption is not valid, you can switch to working with term instead of termID, but this will cause the files on the disk to be larger and the whole process to be slower. It can be assumed that the collection of documents does not change and that the data corresponds to the disk of one computer. But in practice, these assumptions are not valid because the documents are changing and like the data is growing – it will not be possible to save them to one computer.$TRANS$
