            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.271000+00:00',
            $TRANS$In the case of steaming, we will get a mouse and a pigeon, meaning that the accuracy will be 2/5. • In a Boolean retrieval system, steaming never lowers recall. True, the denominator will not change, the denominator is not related to what came back, but to what is relevant, and there is a chance that the denominator will go up. According to the example above: the recall without steaming will give us back 1/2 while the recall with the steaming will give us back 1, so this is true, meaning that with the steaming it will not be lower.$TRANS$
