            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "סיכום למבחן אחזור מידע (1).pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "f6d20139-0dd8-4492-abed-7df9df2d0ad0", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808", "create_date": "2025-08-26T11:29:00.257Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/de0ff05457533c93fdf3e0d1cdd0f808/data/1756207659351-0c8cd1917d00e951630029e4978e9147.pdf", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: Jaccard coefficient, k-grams, Levenshtein Distance, רצפים, הבדלים"}}'::jsonb,
            '2025-08-26T11:29:00.257000+00:00',
            $TRANS$The coefficient checks for an overlap between two groups A and B: 푗푎푐푐푎푟푑 푐표푒푓푓푖푐푖푒푛푡= |퐴∩퐵| |퐴푈퐵|   When the groups are sorted, the complexity depends on the size of the longest list. In our example: A= all the k-grams of the query $l lo or rd d$ B= all the k-grams of a word from the dictionary, take the word border: $b bo or rd de er r$ Levenshtein Distance, a measure of the differences between two sequences (will be the algorithm). The metric for checking for differences between two words is the minimum number of actions performed on a single letter, which are required to turn one word into another.$TRANS$
