            $TRANS$In the social sciences, an accepted measure of consensus is called Kappa:1 The calculation was made after we found the IDCG in the ideal table, for a search engine 1. )(1)()( EPAP kappa − − = For the purpose of understanding, we will repeat the probability. The purpose of the function is to quantitatively express the probability that a certain event will occur. We will mark with P(C) the probability that event C will happen. We will define a sample space Ω – the sum of all possible outcomes. Example of the sample space = possible outcomes of a dice roll: Ω = {1,2,3,4,5,6} We define the event C: the cube fell on an even result - C={2,4,6}.$TRANS$
